{"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials","title":"Guides & Tutorials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftOptimize\/documentation\/SwiftOptimize\/HyperparameterTuning","doc:\/\/SwiftOptimize\/documentation\/SwiftOptimize\/ParallelModelSelection"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Cross-validation is essential for estimating the out-of-sample prediction error and hyperparameter tuning without data leakage. ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiftOptimize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" generates zero-allocation index pairs ","type":"text"},{"code":"(trainIndices, validationIndices)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead of duplicating dataset matrices in memory.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Index-Based Split Architecture","anchor":"Index-Based-Split-Architecture","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each split strategy implements deterministic or seeded index generation:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["Dataset (N samples)","┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐","│ Fold 1: [ Val (20%) ] [                Train (80%)        ] │","│ Fold 2: [ Train (20%) ] [ Val (20%) ] [ Train (60%)       ] │","│ Fold 3: [ Train (40%) ] [ Val (20%) ] [ Train (40%)       ] │","│ Fold 4: [ Train (60%) ] [ Val (20%) ] [ Train (20%)       ] │","│ Fold 5: [                Train (80%)        ] [ Val (20%) ] │","└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"text":"1. Standard K-Fold Cross-Validation","anchor":"1-Standard-K-Fold-Cross-Validation","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"KFold","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" splits continuous regression data or balanced observations into $K$ contiguous or randomized partitions.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Foundation","import SwiftDataFrame","import SwiftOptimize","import SwiftML","","\/\/ 1. Prepare synthetic features and targets","let sampleCount = 100","let featureCount = 4","let X = (0..<sampleCount).map { row in","    (0..<featureCount).map { col in Double(row * featureCount + col) * 0.05 }","}","let y = X.map { row in row.reduce(0.0, +) * 1.5 + 2.0 }","","\/\/ 2. Configure 5-fold cross-validation with a fixed random seed","let kfold = try KFold(nSplits: 5, shuffle: true, seed: 42)","let splits = try kfold.split(features: X, targets: y)","","print(\"Generated \\(splits.count) validation folds.\")","","\/\/ 3. Train and evaluate linear regressors across folds","var mseScores: [Double] = []","","for (foldIndex, fold) in splits.enumerated() {","    let trainX = fold.trainFeatures","    let trainY = fold.trainTargets","    let valX = fold.valFeatures","    let valY = fold.valTargets","    ","    let model = LinearRegression(learningRate: 0.01, epochs: 200)","    try await model.fit(features: trainX, targets: trainY)","    ","    let predictions = try await model.predict(features: valX)","    let mse = Metrics.meanSquaredError(yTrue: valY, yPred: predictions)","    mseScores.append(mse)","    ","    print(\"Fold \\(foldIndex + 1): MSE = \\(String(format: \"%.4f\", mse))\")","}","","let meanMSE = mseScores.reduce(0.0, +) \/ Double(mseScores.count)","print(\"Average Cross-Validation MSE: \\(String(format: \"%.4f\", meanMSE))\")"]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"text":"2. Stratified K-Fold for Classification","anchor":"2-Stratified-K-Fold-for-Classification","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"StratifiedKFold","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ensures that every validation fold preserves the exact class label distribution proportions of the entire dataset. This is critical for imbalanced target classes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftOptimize","import SwiftML","","\/\/ 1. Dataset with imbalanced binary classes (80% Class 0, 20% Class 1)","let features = (0..<100).map { i in [Double(i), Double(i * 2)] }","let labels = (0..<100).map { $0 < 80 ? 0.0 : 1.0 }","","\/\/ 2. Initialize Stratified K-Fold","let stratifiedKF = try StratifiedKFold(nSplits: 5, shuffle: true, seed: 123)","let folds = try stratifiedKF.split(features: features, targets: labels)","","for (idx, fold) in folds.enumerated() {","    let valLabels = fold.valTargets.map { Int($0) }","    let class1Count = valLabels.filter { $0 == 1 }.count","    let class0Count = valLabels.filter { $0 == 0 }.count","    ","    print(\"Fold \\(idx + 1): Class 0 = \\(class0Count), Class 1 = \\(class1Count) (Ratio: \\(Double(class1Count)\/Double(valLabels.count)))\")","}"]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"level":2,"text":"3. Expanding-Window TimeSeriesSplit","anchor":"3-Expanding-Window-TimeSeriesSplit","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For temporal and sequential datasets, standard random cross-validation introduces data leakage (evaluating on historical data after training on future observations). ","type":"text"},{"code":"TimeSeriesSplit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" creates expanding historical training windows with forward-looking validation sets.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftOptimize","import SwiftForecast","","let timeSeriesData = (0..<120).map { i in Double(i) * 1.2 + sin(Double(i) * 0.2) }","","let tsSplit = try TimeSeriesSplit(nSplits: 4, maxTrainSize: nil)","let temporalFolds = try tsSplit.split(features: timeSeriesData.map { [$0] }, targets: timeSeriesData)","","for (foldIndex, fold) in temporalFolds.enumerated() {","    print(\"Fold \\(foldIndex + 1): Train \\(fold.trainTargets.count) pts -> Val \\(fold.valTargets.count) pts\")","}"]},{"name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Performance Tip:"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Always access data via index arrays (","type":"text"},{"code":"trainIndices.map { X[$0] }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") rather than cloning full matrices up front. This keeps memory footprints proportional to the active batch size.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftoptimize\/crossvalidationfolds"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftOptimize\/documentation\/SwiftOptimize\/CrossValidationFolds","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"title":"Cross-Validation Strategies","modules":[{"name":"SwiftOptimize"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Evaluate model stability and generalization performance across dataset splits using ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KFold"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StratifiedKFold"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeSeriesSplit"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftOptimize\/documentation\/SwiftOptimize"]]},"references":{"doc://SwiftOptimize/documentation/SwiftOptimize":{"title":"SwiftOptimize","url":"\/documentation\/swiftoptimize","role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftOptimize\/documentation\/SwiftOptimize","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"AutoML, Cross-Validation Folds & Hyperparameter Tuning."}]},"doc://SwiftOptimize/documentation/SwiftOptimize/ParallelModelSelection":{"title":"Concurrent Model Selection & Cross-Validation","url":"\/documentation\/swiftoptimize\/parallelmodelselection","role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftOptimize\/documentation\/SwiftOptimize\/ParallelModelSelection","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Harness all available Apple Silicon CPU and GPU cores using structured Swift Concurrency "},{"code":"TaskGroup","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" primitives.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftOptimize/documentation/SwiftOptimize/HyperparameterTuning":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Automate model exploration and parameter optimization with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GridSearchCV"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RandomizedSearchCV"},{"type":"text","text":", and the intelligent "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AutoML"},{"type":"text","text":" model selector."}],"title":"Hyperparameter Tuning & AutoML Engine","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swiftoptimize\/hyperparametertuning","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftOptimize\/documentation\/SwiftOptimize\/HyperparameterTuning","role":"article"}}}